  Versions are not licensed under this License; the use of any
  distributed Unreleased Version (for example, a shipping binary) is
  governed by the Suisei End User License Agreement, a separate
  contract.

  "Private Use" means using, building, copying, and modifying a
  Released Version, and any Derivative Work based on it, for your own
  purposes, without making the Released Version, or any Derivative
  Work based on it, in whole or in part, available to any third
  party. Keeping a fork on your own machine, or in a repository or
  other storage that only you can access, is Private Use. Publishing
  to a publicly accessible repository or site, selling, renting, or
  otherwise transferring it to others is not Private Use.

  "Commercial Use" means use of Suisei or a Derivative Work primarily
  intended for or directed toward commercial advantage, monetary
  compensation, or revenue-generating activity, or for the internal
  operations of a for-profit business, regardless of Your legal form
  or of whether any fee is charged.

  "Derivative Work" means a modification, adaptation, or fork of a
  Released Version, including any copy that contains your changes.
  Consistent with Section 6, the term does not include User Works or
  Independent Works.

  "User Works" means software, content, code, documents, binaries, or
  other materials that are written, edited, compiled, built,
  analyzed, linked, or otherwise created or processed using Suisei.

  "Independent Works" means works developed independently of Suisei,
  including plugins, extensions, language servers, tools, scripts, or
  other programs, that communicate or interoperate with Suisei solely
  through a documented API, IPC interface, command-line interface,
  plugin interface, or other public interface.

  "Third-Party Components" means third-party software, libraries,
  assets, fonts, or other materials included in or distributed with
  Suisei that are identified as being subject to their own licence
  terms.

  "You" means any individual or legal entity exercising rights under
  this License.

